Or you could do it the other way around. Get nethack to recognize the
events it gets from X, so it can translate them to move commands.

A better solution than this one would be to #override the correct keys
in your Nethack.ad or .XDefaults file. However, this doesn't work for
the current Nethack version because of something or other. 

As usual, if you do install this, you're on your own. You have to set
nethack to numpadmode. You have to set up X to return the correct
events for the cursor keys, here's the section from my .xmodmaprc file.
This is very machine dependant. I'm using Sparcstations.

Also, this could break something else. Bad luck.

Good luck.

--
diff oldX11/winX.c X11/winX.c
23a24
> #include <X11/keysym.h>
1282a1284,1285
>     KeySym ks;
> 
1288c1291,1305
< 			   (KeySym *)0, (XComposeStatus *)0);
---
> 			   &ks, (XComposeStatus *)0);
> 
>     switch(ks)
>       {
>       case XK_Begin: return '7';
>       case XK_End: return '1';
>       case XK_Prior: return '9';
>       case XK_Next: return '3';
>       case XK_Up: return '8';
>       case XK_Down: return '2';
>       case XK_Left: return '4';
>       case XK_Right: return '6';
>       case XK_Home: return '5';
>       }
